sequenceDiagram
    actor "Flutter Mobile Client" as FlutterMobileClient
    participant "Backend Host (ASP.NET Core)" as BackendHostASPNETCore
    actor "Users Module" as UsersModule
    participant "Primary Database" as PrimaryDatabase

    activate BackendHostASPNETCore
    FlutterMobileClient->>BackendHostASPNETCore: 1. PUT /api/v1/users/me Content-Type: application/json Authorization: Bearer <jwt>
    BackendHostASPNETCore-->>FlutterMobileClient: 200 OK or Error Response (400, 401, 500)
    BackendHostASPNETCore->>BackendHostASPNETCore: 1.1. Middleware: Authenticate and Authorize Request
    BackendHostASPNETCore-->>BackendHostASPNETCore: Principal with UserID or 401 Unauthorized
    activate UsersModule
    BackendHostASPNETCore->>UsersModule: 1.2. Sends UpdateUserProfileCommand via MediatR
    UsersModule-->>BackendHostASPNETCore: Updated User Profile DTO or Exception
    BackendHostASPNETCore->>FlutterMobileClient: 1.3. HTTP 200 OK {   "userId": "...   "displayName": "New User Name" }
    FlutterMobileClient->>FlutterMobileClient: 2. Update local state and refresh UI

    note over UsersModule: Business Rule Enforcement: The system ensures a user can only update their own profile by extract...
    note over UsersModule: CQRS Pattern: This flow represents the 'Command' side of CQRS. The UpdateUserProfileCommand encap...
    note over BackendHostASPNETCore: Exception Handling: A global exception handling middleware in the Host is configured to catch spe...

    deactivate UsersModule
    deactivate BackendHostASPNETCore
